{"id": 7, "ok": true, "cmd": "implicit", "ucas": "implicit x^2 + y^2 = 1 for y wrt x", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "implicit", "var": "x", "function": "y", "derivative": "-x/y", "headline": "on the curve x^2 + y^2 - 1 = 0, y as a function of x:", "details": ["dy/dx = -F_x/F_y = -x/y", "holds where F_y = 2y != 0 (the implicit function theorem: there y is locally a differentiable function of x)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "matches the slope of the curve (points solved by bisection and Newton) at 12 points (max relative difference 2e-12)"}], "files": [], "text": "on the curve x^2 + y^2 - 1 = 0, y as a function of x:\n  dy/dx = -F_x/F_y = -x/y\n  holds where F_y = 2y != 0 (the implicit function theorem: there y is locally a differentiable function of x)\n  check: matches the slope of the curve (points solved by bisection and Newton) at 12 points (max relative difference 2e-12)\n"}
{"id": 8, "ok": true, "cmd": "continuous", "ucas": "continuous sum(i, 1, n, i)", "structured": false, "result": {"text": "  note: n is a bound of sum: taken as int in 0..100\nsum(i, 1, n, i)\n  the sum ≈ ∫ i di from 1 to n, plus Euler-Maclaurin corrections\n  ∫ i di = i^2/2 + C\n  integral: real(n)^2/2 - 0.5\n  + (g(lo) + g(hi))/2: real(n)^2/2 + (real(n) + 1)/2 - 0.5\n  + (g'(hi) - g'(lo))/12 - (g'''(hi) - g'''(lo))/720 (evaluated below)\n  measured against the sum (relative error):\n      at                       exact          integral    + endpoint  + g', g''' \n      n=0                      0              -           -           -          \n      n=20                     210            0.05        0           0          \n      n=40                     820            0.025       0           0          \n      n=60                     1830           0.017       0           0          \n      n=80                     3240           0.013       0           0          \n      n=100                    5050           0.01        0           0          \n"}, "notes": [{"kind": "rule", "text": "n is a bound of sum: taken as int in 0..100"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  note: n is a bound of sum: taken as int in 0..100\nsum(i, 1, n, i)\n  the sum ≈ ∫ i di from 1 to n, plus Euler-Maclaurin corrections\n  ∫ i di = i^2/2 + C\n  integral: real(n)^2/2 - 0.5\n  + (g(lo) + g(hi))/2: real(n)^2/2 + (real(n) + 1)/2 - 0.5\n  + (g'(hi) - g'(lo))/12 - (g'''(hi) - g'''(lo))/720 (evaluated below)\n  measured against the sum (relative error):\n      at                       exact          integral    + endpoint  + g', g''' \n      n=0                      0              -           -           -          \n      n=20                     210            0.05        0           0          \n      n=40                     820            0.025       0           0          \n      n=60                     1830           0.017       0           0          \n      n=80                     3240           0.013       0           0          \n      n=100                    5050           0.01        0           0          \n"}
